- docs/proposals/LANGUAGE_AND_COMPILER_ENHANCEMENTS.md:305: A read-only mapping does not guarantee immutable contents: another process can overwrite the backing file without truncating it. Even `MAP_PRIVATE` leaves visibility of subsequent file changes unspecified. The proposed immutable `&[u8]` therefore needs a content-stability premise or snapshot mechanism, beyond the stated truncation/SIGBUS premise. Otherwise validation witnesses can become stale while the view remains live. ([mmap documentation](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/mmap.2.html))

- docs/proposals/LANGUAGE_AND_COMPILER_ENHANCEMENTS.md:343: Empty `with()` and absence of `&mut` do not justify `memory(none)`: a function can read caller memory through `&T`. Calling it before and after changing the referent can produce different results, while this attribute permits optimizations that ignore that dependency. Require separate evidence excluding observable memory reads; read-only access needs a weaker memory attribute. ([LLVM reference](https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#function-attributes))

- docs/proposals/LANGUAGE_AND_COMPILER_ENHANCEMENTS.md:365: The modulo rule contradicts `Scalar.checked .rem`, which uses `Int.tmod` and preserves the dividend’s sign under OD114. For signed inputs, `-1 % 3 = -1`, despite `d > 0`. Restrict this rule to unsigned or proved nonnegative dividends; as written, it cannot be proved against `Scalar`.

- docs/proposals/LANGUAGE_AND_COMPILER_ENHANCEMENTS.md:367: `lo ≤ hi` alone does not make the midpoint expression safe for signed machine integers. With `i8` bounds `lo = -128` and `hi = 127`, `hi - lo` overflows before the shift. The transfer rule needs unsigned/nonnegative bounds or additional representability evidence before it can discharge the operation’s safety obligation.
